      "hints": [
        "For $y = 3\\cos 2x$, range is $[-3, 3]$.",
        "For $2y + \\frac{3x}{\\pi} = 5 \\implies y = \\frac{5}{2} - \\frac{3x}{2\\pi}$, evaluate at $x = 0$ ($y = 2.5$) and $x = 2\\pi$ ($y = -0.5$)."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Determine the extrema for the trigonometric curve $y = 3\\cos 2x$ on $[0, 2\\pi]$:\n$$\\text{Smallest value} = -3, \\quad \\text{Largest value} = 3 \\quad (-3 \\le y \\le 3)$$",
        "Determine the extrema for the linear function $y = \\frac{5}{2} - \\frac{3}{2\\pi}x$ on $[0, 2\\pi]$:\n$$\\text{At } x = 0: \\quad y = \\frac{5}{2} - 0 = \\frac{5}{2} = 2.5$$\n$$\\text{At } x = 2\\pi: \\quad y = \\frac{5}{2} - \\frac{3(2\\pi)}{2\\pi} = \\frac{5}{2} - 3 = -\\frac{1}{2} = -0.5$$\n$$\\text{Smallest value} = -\\frac{1}{2}, \\quad \\text{Largest value} = \\frac{5}{2}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Function Extrema": "States curve extrema $-3$ and $3$ (B1). States line smallest value $-1/2$ (B1) and largest value $5/2$ (B1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
